{{History of Okaiken}}
{{Short description|Okaiken's neutral, humanitarian role in the Wolffrean War}}
'''Sanese involvement in the Wolffrean War''' has been strictly limited, humanitarian in character, and deliberately separated from the war's military campaigns. Since the war began in April 2021, [[Okaiken]] has not been a belligerent: it has joined no coalition, conducted no operations against any party, and supplied no weapons to any side. The only deployment of the [[Sanese Imperial Forces]] in the theatre is the Escort Flotilla, which protects Sanese-flagged merchant ships chartered to carry refugees out of the war zone as part of the [[Adonian Community]]-managed sealift.

The government of Prime Minister [[Kousuke Ikazaki]] describes the position as neutrality with a humanitarian exception: Okaiken is willing to evacuate refugees, and unwilling to fight the war. Foreign Minister [[Kenichi Mori]] stated the principle during the debate on [[Adonian Community Resolution 4940]]: "Okaiken will not vote for a war it does not intend to fight."

Beneath the humanitarian commitment lies a deep institutional suspicion of the [[Adonian Community Military]] (ACM). Sanese security policy since 1984 — the year after the [[Adonian Community Mission for Lacashe]], in which 925 Sanese personnel served under a Community command in an intervention that ended with the collapse of the host government — has been governed by the [[Ninth Amendment]] to the [[Constitution of Okaiken]], which confines the armed forces to the defence of the archipelago and reserves the protection of Sanese assets and allies to Okaiken's own judgment. Every element of Okaiken's wartime conduct in 2026 — its votes in the [[Adonian Assembly]], the [[Emergency Maritime Civilian Protection Act]], and the drafting of [[Adonian Community Resolution 4942D|Resolution 4942D]] — rests on that settlement.

== Background ==
{{Main|Okaiken-Wolffrea relations}}
Okaiken has no territory, alliance, or strategic commitment in [[Northwestern Kaftia]]. Its interests in the [[Wolffrean War]] are those of a distant maritime nation: a large Sanese-flagged merchant marine whose hulls and crews work the world's sea lanes, and a refugee catastrophe — more than seventeen million people displaced, over fourteen million of them abroad — that has overwhelmed the neighbouring states of the region.

Relations with Wolffrea itself have been cold for two generations. Okaiken supported the suspension of Wolffrea's credentials in the Adonian Community in 1968, and the bilateral record since — sanctions enforcement, maritime confrontations, and a running series of criminal and commercial disputes — is among the poorest Okaiken maintains with any state. The war did not change the relationship; it removed what little remained of it.

== Neutrality and the Assembly record ==
Okaiken's votes in the Adonian Assembly during the October 2026 crisis followed a consistent pattern: support for humanitarian and political measures, refusal of military ones. Okaiken voted in favour of [[Adonian Community Resolution 4935|Resolution 4935]], funding the refugee evacuation through [[Alwana]]; abstained on [[Adonian Community Resolution 4936|4936]], which would have sanctioned [[Sindewand]] for closing its borders to White Wolffrean refugees; voted in favour of [[Adonian Community Resolution 4938|4938]], sanctioning [[Bonande]] for the occupation of [[Mabanda]]; voted against [[Adonian Community Resolution 4939|4939]], which proposed a unified AC ground peacekeeping force; abstained on [[Adonian Community Resolution 4940|4940]], authorising the [[Joint Working Group for Peace in Northern Kaftia]] (JWG-PNK) to conduct air and naval strikes outside AC joint command; and voted in favour of [[Adonian Community Resolution 4941|4941]], suspending Bonande and [[Yaweka]].

The record has been read as the institutional expression of the Ninth Amendment: Okaiken will pay for the rescue, and will not underwrite the war.

== The sealift and the Escort Flotilla ==
In September 2026, as the refugee sealift out of the [[Pfein Sea]] reached a triage scale of roughly ten thousand embarks a day, Okaiken chartered eleven Sanese-flagged commercial ships to the Adonian Community evacuation and assigned two destroyers of the SIF's Escort Flotilla — including the ''[[ISN Shirakumo]]'' — and a supply ship to protect them, sailing within the AC-managed evacuation operation. When Wolffrea closed its ports to AC ships on 26 September, the fleet relocated to Alwana, which hosts 5.2 million refugees.

On 16 October, during fighting between coalition aircraft and Bonandian coastal guns around Mabanda, shore fire struck the Sanese-flagged ferry ''[[Aozora Maru]]'', damaging the ship and injuring three crew members. The attack — the first on a Sanese hull in the war — transformed Okaiken from a distant contributor into a directly affected state, and set off the domestic and diplomatic events of the following week. Behind the scenes, the Sanese government had been quietly passing the schedule and coordinates of refugee sailings to both the coalition headquarters at [[Joint Base Ajowa]] and, through [[Breisland]], to the Wolffrean government, so that neither side would fire on civilian ferries by mistake; when that channel leaked to the press on 20 October, both sides accused the intermediaries of passing targeting intelligence, and the arrangement collapsed.

== Domestic authorisation ==
{{Main|October 2026 Diet debate on the Wolffrean War|October 2026 Diet emergency resolution on the Wolffrean War}}
The ''Aozora Maru'' attack placed Okaiken's neutrality under domestic pressure, and the Ikazaki Cabinet answered it in statute. An emergency debate of the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken|House of Commoners]] convened on 23 October and continued through the following day, when the Diet passed a legislative package centred on the Emergency Maritime Civilian Protection Act (EMCPA). The Act writes the flotilla's rules of engagement into Sanese law: escort warships may shoot down incoming fire aimed at an evacuation ship and may disable the specific weapon that attacks a convoy, and may not conduct pre-emptive strikes or join offensive operations. On the night of 24 October the House adopted an emergency resolution directing the government to pursue protection of the sealift in the Adonian Community, by 437 votes to 18.

The government described the package as the Ninth Amendment and the Fortress State doctrine given statutory form: a state that will not fight the war must be able to guarantee that it cannot be dragged into it.

== Scepticism of the ACM ==
Sanese policy toward the Adonian Community Military is best described as institutional scepticism, and its foundation is the Lacashe account.

In 1981–1983, Okaiken contributed 925 personnel to the Adonian Community Mission for Lacashe, an intervention authorised to stabilise a domestic crisis that instead engaged the armed forces of the host state, took casualties on all three sides, and ended with the collapse of the Lacashian government. The mission is remembered in Lacashe as the turning point toward constitutional order; it is remembered in Okaiken as the demonstration that a Community command can carry a contributing state's forces into combat and regime collapse regardless of what the contributing state intended. The Ninth Amendment, ratified the following year, is the settlement of that account: Sanese forces would defend the archipelago, protect Sanese assets and allies, and fight nothing else.

The war in Wolffrea has tested each clause. The Secretariat's direction of the ACM — including the reinforcement of the evacuation mission with an additional AC Navy fleet — is noted in Okami without enthusiasm; the gathering of coalition amphibious forces near the [[Strait of Sindewand]] is watched with considerably more alarm. When the delegation of [[Louyan]] observed in October 2026 that self-defence rules for the sealift already exist and are defined by the admirals, it stated, from Okaiken's perspective, precisely the problem: rules for the protection of Sanese ships, written by a command Okaiken does not control, for an operation Okaiken did not design. The EMCPA exists to answer that problem — the rules governing Sanese escorts are Sanese law, adopted by the Sanese Diet.

The same scepticism shaped the investigation provisions of Resolution 4942D. The ''Aozora Maru'' was struck while sailing in an AC-managed operation, and Okaiken pressed for the inquiry to be conducted by the [[Adonian Community Observer Mission in Northern Kaftia]] and Secretariat investigators rather than by the ACM's own operational chain, on the principle that a military command does not investigate its own operation.

== The government response of 25 October ==
By 25 October the demand that the Escort Flotilla be brought under an AC or coalition command had been pressed from three directions — the Burawan objection through the JWG-PNK, the Jarin amendment request, and the démarche of the Zong ambassador — and the notice of Louyan's motion to dismiss Resolution 4942D had added the argument that the Assembly should not legislate for the military at all. That afternoon the Ministry of Foreign Affairs issued a formal response in the name of Foreign Minister Mori. Its operative passages:

<blockquote>
The Government of Okaiken reiterates that its position has not changed since the first day of the war. Okaiken is not a belligerent and will not become one. Its forces are in the Pfein Sea for one purpose: that refugees leave the war alive. The ferries will sail, and the escorts will sail with them.

The Ninth Amendment reserves to Okaiken alone the protection of Sanese lives and Sanese property. A Sanese ship does not cease to be a Sanese ship because she is chartered to the Community's lift, and a Sanese crew does not cease to be a Sanese crew because their ship flies a mission pennant. Whether a hull is leased to the Community or is not, the duty of protecting it — and the right — belongs to Okaiken, and it is not a delegable duty.

Okaiken coordinates with the Secretariat, as it has from the first day. Coordination is not command, and participation is not subordination.

Sanese forces have served under a Community command once in the history of the state. Nine hundred and twenty-five of them went to Lacashe under a flag that was not their own, and the mission they were sent to steady ended with the fall of a government and the dead of three armies. The Ninth Amendment is the settlement of that account, and the account stays settled.

Okaiken is an independent nation. It is bound by the treaties it has signed, and by nothing else — not by the Community's goals in Wolffrea, and not by the coalition's. The goals the coalition pursues, and the means the Community's military commands judge necessary, are not Okaiken's goals and are not Okaiken's means, and the Sanese people are not bound to them.
</blockquote>

== Reception ==
The statement was reported as the government's fullest public formulation of the Fortress State doctrine, and the first to invoke the Lacashe mission by name in a sitting minister's delivery. The sovereignty framing drew support across the Diet's opposition benches, where the [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Liberal Democratic Party]] had pressed the government to give the Ninth Amendment a more assertive reading. In [[Areza]], diplomatic reporting read the Lacashe passage as addressed less to the coalition than to the Secretariat itself — a warning that Okaiken's cooperation with the ACM's evacuation fleet should not be mistaken for confidence in the ACM's command.

